      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MRS BULL (7) doesn't boast the best strike rate but finds the right race today. Made up many lengths to finish fourth last start over 1300m at Bathurst. In the money at 12 of 19 runs over the mile. Drops 6kgs after the claim on the last run so despite a class rise she looks a terrific chance. LIKE LUKEY (1) was beaten just 2.4 lengths in a BM82 over this trip at Tamworth two back. Fair effort last time over 1800m but coming back to 1600m should see the best in her. SHAGGY ROGERS (2) had a five-week break and a change of trainer before a return to form recently, beaten a whisker in open company over 1280m at Gilgandra. Strips fitter and will appreciate a bit more ground today. YIASOU (3) failed by a whisker in an attempt to chalk up the hat trick last start over 1400m at Tamworth. Likely leader who will give a sight - the last 100m is the concern. COOMA HUT (8) has filled a top three spot at all three tries over the mile. In the mix on a seven-day back-up.",
